::ingredients

(onion, cut into quarter moons) 6-7
(butter) 1 stick
(olive oil) 1/2 cup
(salt) to taste
(baguette, sliced) 1
(chicken broth) 1 can
(garlic, finely chopped) 3 cloves
(brown sugar) 1/4 cup
(balsamic vinegar) to taste
(Worcestershire sauce) to taste
(soy sauce) to taste
(beef broth) 64oz
(bay leaf) 2-3
(cheese, melty, preferably guereye or swiss) as needed

::equipment

(Dutch oven)
(strainer)
(wooden spoon)
(oven)

::instructions

(onion) + (butter) + (olive oil) some + (salt) <sweat, Dutch oven, covered, medium-low, ~2h, stir and gradually increase heat and stirring>
    <strain, when soft and shrunken and covered with juices, collect juice>
{onion juice} <brush, both sides of baguette slices>
(onion) <cook, return to pot, medium-high, uncovered>
    + (chicken broth) <deglaze, incrementally, stir frequently, avoid mush>
    + (garlic) + (brown sugar) + (balsamic vinegar) + (Worcestershire sauce) + (soy sauce) <caramelise, allow drying and fond between liquid additions, slowly deglaze with wooden spoon>
    + (beef broth) + (bay leaf) <simmer, covered, medium>
(baguette) <toast, 400°F>
    + (cheese) <broil, until melted>
<serve, pour soup over bread or float bread on soup>

